#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ccad579-7ffd-5028-82c9-8be517c44ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303432} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a96f69-83dc-57ab-88b1-de0764e272b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,2,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303669} {:answer/id #uuid "dc88a9e0-a58d-507d-8dbf-f29575569623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303833} {:answer/id #uuid "f8782171-7da4-599e-a483-393f0200a20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,8,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304012} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f6c3e0-0705-5423-bdeb-301d579540f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ccad579-7ffd-5028-82c9-8be517c44ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303432} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0993881-1ebc-59b3-9c71-cbd4dfde3c44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c249fd8c-dcff-5201-89e1-bb6d2a206072" :question/math-academy-id "q-33201" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-4⟩+t⟨2,4,3⟩,\\,Π:4x+3y+4z-60=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+4z-60 & =0 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z & =60 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ 4(3+2t)+3(4t)+4(-4+3t) & =60 \\\\ 12+8t+12t-16+12t & =60 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(2),4(2),-4+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,8,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,8,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee24fdf4-e1ee-5f88-bc78-1cd69107c3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402258} {:answer/id #uuid "3cff9213-8332-5106-9a38-96d7ec4a4378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,5,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402259} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7ebdfb-49aa-56f4-a0ad-f4d48aa68b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402260} {:answer/id #uuid "6adfa3c5-c5cd-56cd-841d-1fd0fc016077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402261} {:answer/id #uuid "cd22fb61-25ce-5f17-bad1-fbd4ce2f0694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd22fb61-25ce-5f17-bad1-fbd4ce2f0694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402262} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9e05243-350c-5a1d-ad1e-5c71c37318cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fc86f8-0368-54eb-a3e0-3cf6b0379332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} {:answer/id #uuid "2143e54b-67d5-5002-957a-3bf88c230ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(24,-11,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483624} {:answer/id #uuid "257b548a-b52d-5b2d-8a2f-57d74b50d39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483630} {:answer/id #uuid "7944f3e7-3b31-5e5a-b5cb-a1562208eb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-13,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483813} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a4f2b9-c6e0-5e67-8ab6-66d592472d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(26,12,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20fc86f8-0368-54eb-a3e0-3cf6b0379332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f90597-4c03-5ae4-b2c2-f42eae091087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12b4f5c6-720f-5c2c-b1e8-295eb7dcb29c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73991" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-2t \\\\ y &=5-3t \\\\ z &=-1+2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x-2y+6z=62.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+6z & =62 \\\\ 3(-2-2t)-2(5-3t)+6(-1+2t) & =62 \\\\ -6-6t-10+6t-6+12t & =62 \\\\ 12t & =84 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=6$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-2(7)=-16 \\\\ y &=5-3(7)=-16 \\\\ z &=-1+2(7)=13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-16,-16,13).$"}]}
